They recounted that it was adapted into a stage musical in 2008, with film and theater actor Oh Man-seok making his directorial debut. Oh was also the lyricist and polished the script. The story centers on two men who are crazy about music: one is a high-school music teacher, Beom-jin, who has broken up with his girlfriend and now sadly eats alone in front of his mirror out of habit; the other is the younger Sae-ki, whose mother left and whose father died in a sudden accident, leaving him an orphan. In this rather dull world, the only thing that makes the two feel alive is music, which offers them their "happy life." Yoo Jun-sang and Im Choon-gil alternated as Beom-jin, and Kim Mu-yeol and Ryan alternated as Sae-ki.